conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8310173Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8399480Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8407698Z ^[[0m
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8408170Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8408649Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8408911Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8409267Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8409874Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8410212Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8410985Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8411468Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8411688Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8412115Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8412704Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8413044Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8413320Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8413444Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8413581Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8413765Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8413913Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8414208Z    can use Nix.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8414317Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8414393Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8414513Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8414738Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8415092Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8419212Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8419328Z I will:
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8419532Z 
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8419754Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8420215Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8420743Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8421049Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8421257Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8421466Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8421764Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8422034Z    /root
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8432605Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8433332Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8443245Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-rebuild (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8443855Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
