flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6236340Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6620050Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6645540Z ^[[0m
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6646310Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6656020Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6656620Z 
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6657000Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6657840Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6658350Z 
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6658670Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6659350Z    if you are ready to continue.
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6659690Z 
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6660550Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [351..360])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 350)^[[0m
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6661440Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6662310Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6663060Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6663350Z 
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6663650Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6664100Z 
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6664460Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6665140Z    can use Nix.
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6665390Z 
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6665570Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6665850Z 
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6666290Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6667050Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6671100Z 
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6671330Z I will:
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6671500Z 
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6672310Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6673430Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6675740Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6676460Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6676950Z  - install Nix in /nix
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6677460Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6678160Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6678820Z    /var/root
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6694310Z  - back up /etc/bashrc to /etc/bashrc.backup-before-nix
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6695120Z  - update /etc/bashrc to include some Nix configuration
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6722740Z  - back up /etc/zshrc to /etc/zshrc.backup-before-nix
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6723200Z  - update /etc/zshrc to include some Nix configuration
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6724740Z  - create a Nix volume and a LaunchDaemon to mount it
flake-check (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.6725710Z  - create a LaunchDaemon (at /Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nixos.nix-daemon.plist) for nix-daemon
