composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8603995Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8616315Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8729751Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8741539Z ^[[0m
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8742202Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8742757Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8743008Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8743355Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8743902Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8748022Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8748493Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8749741Z    if you are ready to continue.
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8750096Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8750868Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8752167Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8753117Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8753832Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8754177Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8754571Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8755082Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8755834Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8756627Z    can use Nix.
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8756904Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8757133Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8757471Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8758093Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8758990Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8759689Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8759986Z I will:
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8760370Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8760734Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8761401Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8761884Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8762306Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8762615Z  - install Nix in /nix
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8762933Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8763374Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8763775Z    /root
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8779795Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8780406Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8792635Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8793208Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8793749Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8795200Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8796222Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8815803Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8816521Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8827862Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8828716Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8829161Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8829380Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8829654Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8830095Z 
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8830467Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8830942Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
composition (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.8831178Z 
