supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.6900090Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7278630Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7301230Z ^[[0m
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7302070Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7302460Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7302650Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7302820Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7303260Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7303580Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7303790Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7304150Z    if you are ready to continue.
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7304310Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7304630Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [351..356])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 350)^[[0m
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7305160Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7305630Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7305960Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7306100Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7306240Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7306470Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7306690Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7307030Z    can use Nix.
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7307140Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7307220Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7307340Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7307580Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7307940Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7322770Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7323130Z I will:
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7323290Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7323830Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7324260Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7325300Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7325650Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7325920Z  - install Nix in /nix
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7326190Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7326590Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7326950Z    /var/root
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7343260Z  - back up /etc/bashrc to /etc/bashrc.backup-before-nix
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7343790Z  - update /etc/bashrc to include some Nix configuration
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7367760Z  - back up /etc/zshrc to /etc/zshrc.backup-before-nix
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7368180Z  - update /etc/zshrc to include some Nix configuration
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7369390Z  - create a Nix volume and a LaunchDaemon to mount it
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7369930Z  - create a LaunchDaemon (at /Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nixos.nix-daemon.plist) for nix-daemon
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7370310Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7370520Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7370860Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7401310Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7401800Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7421900Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7422560Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7422890Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7423070Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7423270Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7423510Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7423700Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7424080Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7424270Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7424340Z If you would like to
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7424580Z see the output, try like this:
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7424760Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7424930Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7425300Z   $ sh ./install-nix
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7425420Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7425440Z 
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7425580Z ^[[32m~~> Fixing any leftover Nix volume state
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7443850Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for any existing Nix volume config
supported-go (macos-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7444410Z and ask for your permission to remove it (so that the installer can
