supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9036176Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9036788Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9037549Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9038117Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9038533Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9038780Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9039085Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9039371Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9039671Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9040155Z    can use Nix.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9040347Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9040471Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9040686Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9041102Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9041999Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9042318Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9042504Z I will:
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9042759Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9043110Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9043643Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9044158Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9044655Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9045030Z  - install Nix in /nix
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9045376Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9046309Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9046770Z    /root
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9056425Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9057104Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9066287Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9067007Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9067337Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-27)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9068260Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
