gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9562714Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9570887Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9655258Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9663011Z ^[[0m
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9663549Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9666217Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9667764Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9668195Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9669246Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9669645Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9670297Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9671067Z    if you are ready to continue.
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9671360Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9671888Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9672860Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9673571Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9674033Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9674270Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9674615Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9674981Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9675699Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9676351Z    can use Nix.
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9676649Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9676840Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9677057Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9677464Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9679034Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9679682Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9680412Z I will:
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9680975Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9681271Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9682035Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9682838Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9683442Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9684137Z  - install Nix in /nix
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9684844Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9685784Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9686500Z    /root
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9687315Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9687956Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9696627Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9697475Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9697827Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9698277Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9698892Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9714345Z 
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9715383Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9723189Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9724172Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9724820Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
gopath-native (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.9725051Z 
