composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.3441640Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4118770Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4154920Z ^[[0m
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4156010Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4156940Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4157420Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4157820Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4158840Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4159460Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4159830Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4160610Z    if you are ready to continue.
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4161080Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4161740Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [351..356])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 350)^[[0m
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4162830Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4163830Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4164640Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4164990Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4165340Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4165900Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4166320Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4167120Z    can use Nix.
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4167520Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4167740Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4168080Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4168650Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4169590Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4192160Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4193130Z I will:
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4193540Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4193970Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4194860Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4196080Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4197090Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4197740Z  - install Nix in /nix
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4198300Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4199140Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4199920Z    /var/root
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4229050Z  - back up /etc/bashrc to /etc/bashrc.backup-before-nix
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4229940Z  - update /etc/bashrc to include some Nix configuration
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4287620Z  - back up /etc/zshrc to /etc/zshrc.backup-before-nix
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4288340Z  - update /etc/zshrc to include some Nix configuration
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4291680Z  - create a Nix volume and a LaunchDaemon to mount it
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4293110Z  - create a LaunchDaemon (at /Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nixos.nix-daemon.plist) for nix-daemon
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4293570Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4293850Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4294100Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4357370Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4358070Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4394620Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4396110Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4397010Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4397440Z 
composition (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:26:56.4398170Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
