supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7113057Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7218171Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7228860Z ^[[0m
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7229673Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7230178Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7230407Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7230613Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7231418Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7231937Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7232753Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7233569Z    if you are ready to continue.
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7233901Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7234569Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7235686Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7236165Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7236511Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7236680Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7236845Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7237104Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7237289Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7238251Z    can use Nix.
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7238477Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7238628Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7238885Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7239337Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7239801Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7243646Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7243803Z I will:
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7244095Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7244414Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7245087Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7245772Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7246415Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7246863Z  - install Nix in /nix
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7247281Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7248032Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7248543Z    /root
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7259533Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7260250Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7271699Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7272246Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7272645Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7274048Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
supported-go (ubuntu-latest, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.7274654Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
