conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1765597Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1862028Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1871707Z ^[[0m
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1872748Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1873688Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1874163Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1874591Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1875702Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1876571Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1877049Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1878214Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1878699Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1879426Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1880396Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1881364Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1882162Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1882751Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1883210Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1883612Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1884139Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1884929Z    can use Nix.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1885229Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1885430Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1885832Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1886416Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1887242Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1887725Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1888020Z I will:
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1888341Z 
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1888729Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1889498Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1890111Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1890633Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1891098Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1891486Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1891990Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1893092Z    /root
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1901157Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1902015Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1910858Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-offline (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:45.1911623Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
