conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1952317Z ^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1952889Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1955341Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1955693Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1955995Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1956717Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1957090Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1957759Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1958437Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1958772Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1959222Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1960120Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1960825Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1961394Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1962090Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1962533Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1962874Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1963135Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1963682Z    can use Nix.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1964181Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1964371Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1964620Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1965007Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1965820Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1966172Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1966350Z I will:
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1966567Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1966942Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1967561Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1968115Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1968689Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1969074Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1969575Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1970289Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1970884Z    /root
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1976721Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1977484Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1987420Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-relock (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1988104Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
