conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7665650Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7665880Z 
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7666030Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7666330Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7666460Z 
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7666730Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [351..356])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 350)^[[0m
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7667150Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7667510Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7667790Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7667910Z 
conformance-update (macos-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:29:03.7668020Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
