outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9439055Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9446820Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9524061Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9532176Z ^[[0m
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9532490Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9532865Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9533066Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9533258Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9541956Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9542350Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9542687Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9543298Z    if you are ready to continue.
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9543488Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9543844Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9544502Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9545072Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9545389Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9545544Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9546653Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9546816Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9546998Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9547253Z    can use Nix.
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9547361Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9547453Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9547559Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9547971Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9548442Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9548618Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9548736Z I will:
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9548844Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9549004Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9549359Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9549820Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9550156Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9550403Z  - install Nix in /nix
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9550647Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9551131Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9551471Z    /root
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9560505Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9560944Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9569529Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9569837Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9570001Z 
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9571747Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
outside-the-sandbox (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:43.9571998Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
