supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.1998868Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2079055Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2088017Z ^[[0m
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2088830Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2089495Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2089779Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2090039Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2091403Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2091896Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2092142Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2092751Z    if you are ready to continue.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2093457Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2094583Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2095347Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2096096Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2096576Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2096818Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2097221Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2097598Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2097909Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2098388Z    can use Nix.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2098661Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2098829Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2099091Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2099578Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2100313Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2100636Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2100820Z I will:
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2101332Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2101604Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2102340Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2102958Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2103659Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2105993Z  - install Nix in /nix
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2106507Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2107021Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2107482Z    /root
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2203955Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2204726Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2215391Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2216323Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2216741Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2217189Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2217780Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2235893Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2237070Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2245698Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2247365Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2247910Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2248332Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2248570Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2248898Z 
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2249152Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
supported-go (ubuntu-24.04-arm, 1-26)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.2249665Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
