conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8644322Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8652670Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8742940Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8752254Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8753115Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8753664Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8753996Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8754297Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8754830Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8755146Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8755897Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8756952Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8757173Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8757663Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8758700Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8759337Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8759811Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8760082Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8760334Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8760655Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8760931Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8761413Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8761562Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8761701Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8761876Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8766604Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8767633Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8772483Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8773006Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8773350Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8773839Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8774382Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8774861Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8775361Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8775721Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8776082Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8776832Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8777257Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8788869Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8796064Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8796983Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8797878Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8798176Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8798543Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8799106Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8815125Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8815783Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8824645Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8825356Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8825851Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8826330Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8826683Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8826990Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8827211Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8827795Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8828052Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8828244Z If you would like to
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8828568Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8828756Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8829053Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8829471Z   $ sh ./install-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8829721Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8829731Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8830021Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8836043Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T04:25:46.8836775Z been installed on this system.
